ervices for individuals, as well as pension, profit-sharing, and employee benefit plan administration services for corporations. Further, the company offers insurance agency services comprising group health care policies and life insurance, and property and casualty insurance products. The company was founded in 1851 and is headquartered in Glens Falls, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David S. DeMarco | CEO, President & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 725 people. Each employee generates $50K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $942 per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Arrow Financial Corporation is a small-cap financial services business with a $716M market cap.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","The business throws off $36M in free cash flow, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.94\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Shareholder yield of 4.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.0% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Price sits 21% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.20805210315754685},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why (AROW) Price Action Is Critical for Tactical Trading","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/134/Why_AROW_Price_Action_Is_Critical_for_Tactical_Trading_110926104602_1794282362.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794282362.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Arrow Financial (NASDAQ:AROW) Given \u201cOverweight\u201d Rating at Piper Sandler","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/arrow-financial-nasdaqarow-given-overweight-rating-at-piper-sandler.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794242568.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Arrow Financial Corp's Dividend Analysis","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/arrow-financial-corps-dividend-analysis-101954083.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794305994.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.718,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Arrow Financial Director Tenee Casac